# Source: https://github.com/GMOD/jbrowse-components/issues/5073
# Symptom: non-UCSC tool (nhmmer) emits a BED-like file prefixed with detailed
#   comment lines that do not follow the UCSC "track"/"browser" format; instead
#   they use arbitrary "# key: value" metadata about the tool run.  JBrowse
#   loads the file but shows no name labels because the comment block interferes
#   with the name column parser.  A validator should flag that comment lines
#   contain non-UCSC-metadata content and may confuse downstream tools.
#					-
#			dir:		-
#			file:		-
#			mode:		-
#			nhmmer		-
#	Gallus_gallus.tblout	--tblout	settings:		-
#	accession	hmmfrom	name	envfrom	+
#			3.4		-
#-------------------	-------	-------	--------------------	------	-
NC_006088.5	1465687	1465847	LFSINE_Vert	36.1	-
NC_006088.5	1521282	1521350	LFSINE_Vert	19.8	-
